@page "/privacy"

<PageTitle>Privacy Policy · Kings of the Card Arena</PageTitle>

<InfoPage Title="Privacy Policy" Updated="@LegalInfo.LastUpdated">
    <p>
        Kings of the Card Arena is run by @LegalInfo.Owner, who is responsible for your data. This page explains what the game
        stores, why, how long it keeps it, and how you can download or delete it.
    </p>

    <h2>What we store</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><b>Your account:</b> your hero name and a hash of your password (never the password itself), plus failed sign-in counts used to lock out password guessing.</li>
        <li>
            <b>Your recovery email, if you add one:</b> used only to send you a link to confirm it and, if you ask, a link to
            reset your password. Only a hash of each link is stored, and links expire within a day.
        </li>
        <li><b>Your hero:</b> class, level, gold, rating, purchases, titles, cosmetics, bounties and your portrait if you upload one.</li>
        <li><b>Your games:</b> boss fights, duels, match history and the daily arena totals they add to (which don't identify anyone).</li>
        <li><b>Sign-in sessions:</b> when each session started and ends. Only a hash of each session token is kept.</li>
        <li>
            <b>Two-factor sign-in, if you turn it on:</b> the secret key your authenticator app shares with the game, the
            time of the last code you used (so it can't be used again), and a hash of each recovery code (never the codes themselves).
        </li>
        <li>
            <b>Admin decisions:</b> if an admin suspends your account, corrects your gold, renames your hero or removes your
            portrait, the game records what was done, when, by which admin and why. A suspension's reason is shown to you
            when you try to sign in. After a rename, your old name is kept so you can still sign in with it.
        </li>
        <li>
            <b>Reports:</b> when you report a hero's name or portrait, the game keeps who reported whom, what for, your note
            and what an admin decided. The hero you report is never told it was you.
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>An email address is optional. We don't ask for your real name, location or payment details, and we don't sell or share your data.</p>

    <h2>Technical data</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <b>Diagnostics:</b> to find bugs and slow spots, the game sends Microsoft Application Insights which screens you open,
            how long pages and requests take, and any errors, tagged with your hero's id (not its name) once you sign in. Your
            IP address is used for an approximate country or city and is not stored.
        </li>
        <li><b>Abuse protection:</b> your IP address is held in memory briefly to limit sign-in attempts and spot duels between two accounts on one network.</li>
        <li><b>Your browser:</b> the game sets no cookies. It saves your sound on/off choice in your browser's local storage, the diagnostics library briefly holds unsent data in session storage, and your sign-in is kept in memory only, so closing the tab signs you out.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Where it lives</h2>
    <p>
        Everything is stored in Microsoft Azure data centers in the United States. Microsoft processes it on our behalf
        to host the game, and sends recovery emails through Azure Communication Services.
    </p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Your account, hero, recovery email, two-factor key and match history: until you delete your hero (or remove the email, or turn two-factor off).</li>
        <li>Finished battles: 30 days. Expired sign-in sessions: 7 days after they end.</li>
        <li>Diagnostics and logs: 30 days.</li>
        <li>Admin decisions about your account: one year, even if you delete your hero, so a decision can be checked if it's questioned.</li>
        <li>Reports: 90 days after an admin deals with them. Reports you made, and reports about you, are deleted with your hero.</li>
        <li>After you delete your hero, copies can remain in database backups and deleted-file storage for up to 7 days, and in diagnostics for up to 30 days, before they're gone for good.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><b>See your data:</b> <b>Your account and data</b> in town downloads a file with everything stored about your hero, including admin decisions about it.</li>
        <li><b>Delete your data:</b> the same place deletes your hero and everything tied to it straight away. Opponents keep their record of duels with you, but your name is removed from it.</li>
        <li>For anything else, such as correcting something, email <a href="@LegalInfo.ContactUrl">@LegalInfo.Contact</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>The game isn't aimed at children under 13, and we don't knowingly keep data about them. If you believe a child has an account, get in touch and it will be removed.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
        If this policy changes, the date above changes with it. See also the <a href="terms">Terms of Service</a> and
        the game's <a href="status">system status</a>.
    </p>
</InfoPage>
